        "role": "user",
        "content": "{\"original_question\":\"I'm considering whether I should start scripting my cooking videos or just go with the flow. What do you think?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"What are the user's past experiences with cooking videos, including any mention of scripting, preparation, or spontaneous approaches?\",\"output_slot\":\"cooking_video_history\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"What are the user's past experiences with cooking videos, including any mention of scripting, preparation, or spontaneous approaches?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"35aed8d7f84569d1e1aa154ada2f991cce28aecf4217b8c3af500c22ce332c33\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"23c8341d5d524bcf17f58ddade3966e85462ab8b9a9a2cc5ea4b3ccfa0633a2b\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"7c70cd9fbbbc0502848f9a1a941f73cb8341a22129c4364d7602f07b9036937a\"},\"variables\":{\"cooking_video_history\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"cooking_video_history\",\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"cooking_video_history\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"cooking_video_history\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_c0aa004f778c06938d6ea97b\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user has no direct past experience with cooking videos, scripting, preparation, or spontaneous approaches in that domain. However, they have extensive related creative experiences: they abandoned writing book reviews because it felt stifling and limiting to creativity (s3), preferring fluid discussions that allow spontaneity (s4). They started a book review blog but lost interest as it became a chore (s13, s14). They dabbled in fan fiction but felt it no longer matched their evolving personal style (s30, s31). They tried creating art based on book themes but it did not resonate (s40, s41). They hosted a podcast episode with an author (s21) and conducted an interview with a debut author (s49), both providing insights into creative processes. Across these experiences, the user consistently values spontaneity, authenticity, and freedom from rigid structures, and has abandoned or lost interest in activities that felt formulaic or obligatory.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s14\",\"s40\",\"s3\",\"s30\",\"s4\",\"s21\",\"s31\",\"s49\",\"s13\",\"s41\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's past creative experiences consistently show a preference for spontaneity and a dislike for rigid scripting or formal structures. They abandoned book reviews and a blog due to feeling stifled, and lost interest in fan fiction and art projects that didn't align with their evolving style. They enjoyed fluid discussions, podcasting, and interviews. These patterns are directly relevant to the question about scripting vs. going with the flow for cooking videos, though no direct cooking video experience is mentioned.\",\"variable\":\"cooking_video_history\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,457,\"User: I also abandoned the idea of writing reviews. I feel that they tend to limit my creativity, as if I am being boxed into a particular format that doesn't allow my thoughts to flow freely. There's something inherently stifling about structuring my feelings and opinions into a rigid framework, filled with guidelines about what to include or omit. \",\"user\",[53]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",457,790,\"Discussions, however, offer a much more fluid space where I can articulate my thoughts just as they come, allowing for spontaneity and genuine enthusiasm to take the lead. It’s fascinating how shifting my focus from written critiques to engaging dialogues can unleash a more authentic appreciation for the literary works that I love.\",\"user\",[53]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",105,455,\"User: I even started a blog about book reviews, but I lost interest quickly. It felt more like a chore at times. I had all these grand ideas about expressing my thoughts on various novels and sharing them with potential readers. However, as the weeks went by, the excitement fizzled out, and it became daunting to even consider writing another post. \",\"user\",[32]],[\"s14\",\"d2\",455,723,\"The joy I initially felt while discussing character arcs and plot twists was overshadowed by the pressure to consistently produce content. It was as if the very act of sharing my passion had turned into an obligation that drained my enthusiasm rather than igniting it.\",\"user\",[32]],[\"s21\",\"d3\",107,381,\"User: I also hosted a podcast episode featuring an author, where we discussed their inspiration and creative process. This particular episode was not just about the mechanics of writing, but also delved into the personal experiences that shape the author's narrative voice. \",\"user\",[160]],[\"s30\",\"d4\",105,381,\"User: I even dabbled in writing fan fiction but felt it didn’t match my personal writing style anymore. I used to enjoy immersing myself in those universes, creating new scenarios and plots that brought my favorite characters to life in ways that hadn’t been explored before. \",\"user\",[40]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",381,768,\"However, as I continued to write, I began to notice a disconnect; my voice seemed to evolve, shifting towards a style that felt more unique to me, and I no longer felt that fan fiction was a suitable canvas. I often found myself reflecting on how fan fiction can be a stepping stone for many writers, allowing them to practice their craft in familiar settings while honing their skills. \",\"user\",[40]],[\"s40\",\"d5\",105,313,\"User: I even tried creating art based on book themes; however, it didn’t resonate much with me. Creating art can be an incredibly personal journey, often reflecting the artist's own experiences and emotions. \",\"user\",[36]],[\"s41\",\"d5\",313,638,\"In this instance, despite the intention behind the artwork, it seems that the connection between the themes of the books and your creative expression did not manifest in a way that felt fulfilling. It's fascinating how sometimes the ideas that spark our imagination in one context fail to ignite the same passion in another. \",\"user\",[36]],[\"s49\",\"d6\",105,505,\"User: I conducted an enlightening interview with a debut author recently, which gave me new insights into the writing process. It was truly inspiring to hear their unique perspective, as they navigated the often daunting world of publishing for the first time. They shared moments of doubt and frustration that resonated deeply with me as someone who has also faced challenges in creative endeavors. \",\"user\",[84]],[\"s181\",\"d7\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 149–151 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s182\",\"d7\",101,107,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s183\",\"d7\",107,499,\"User: I'm assisting with literacy programs and organizing community events to promote reading. It's really rewarding. ])\\n\\nUser: I also restarted my book blog, and I'm beginning a series focused on emotional responses to literature. This has been a journey of rediscovery for me, as I dive back into a world of words that often encapsulate feelings I experience but have trouble articulating. \",\"user\",[149,150]],[\"s184\",\"d7\",499,805,\"The intricate relationship between text and emotion is fascinating, especially how different narratives can evoke specific memories and feelings from my past. It's almost like each book becomes a vessel, carrying not just the author's intention but my own reflections and personal narratives 